{
  "id": "u12-l05",
  "unit": "u12-have-to",
  "title": "I couldn't, I'll be able to",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**'Couldn't' = পারিনি.** As in **করিনি**, **-নি** makes the past negative: **আমি আসতে পারিনি** 'I couldn't come'. For সে it's **পারেনি**. You'll also hear **পারলাম না**; both are fine.\n\n**'Will be able to' = পারব, পারবে, পারবেন**, with the future endings you know: **আমি সাতটায় আসতে পারব** 'I can come at seven'.\n\n**পারব না** 'I won't be able to' is how to say no to a plan: **দুঃখিত, আমি আজ আসতে পারব না।** 'Sorry, I can't come today.'\n\nEnglish 'can' about a later time is usually **পারব / পারবে** in Bengali.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "parini",
      "bn": "পারিনি",
